  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Demand remains pressured by a challenging housing and remodeling backdrop, with particular weakness in core sanitaryware products and softer activity among certain homebuilder customers. Offsetting this, the company’s diversified product lines—notably bath furniture and shower systems—are gaining traction through new customer wins and improved market penetration, demonstrating resilience outside traditional categories.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is leaning into its Brands, Products and Channels (“BPC”) strategy, and early signs suggest the shift is generating momentum. Investment in new product introductions and channel expansion is helping the business navigate macro headwinds, even as overall revenue remains under strain. The narrative conveys cautious optimism that strategic diversification is taking hold, though the company is still operating at a loss and credibility remains tied to execution in a difficult environment.",
